  "description": "A parametric CHANDELIER on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nDROP IT ON A NODE and it hangs there from the ceiling height you set, the chain taking up whatever is left above the column.\n\nALMOST NOTHING HERE IS A BOX, so almost nothing here is a quad. A chandelier is a chain, a column, a set of arms sloping down and out, a cup and a candle on each — every one of them a SOLID ABOUT AN ARBITRARY AXIS, which is exactly what a Tube row is for. The arms are the interesting case: they run from the column out to the candle position AND downward by the arm drop, so their axis is tilted in three dimensions, and a tilted segment needs no special case because the perpendicular frame is derived from the segment itself.\n\nTIERS AND ARMS ARE ONE BROADCAST. `kron(arange(tiers), ones(arms,1))` gives every arm its tier and `kron(ones(tiers,1), arange(arms))` its position within that tier, so a 6-arm single tier and a 3-tier 16-arm frame are the same six lines. Each tier is smaller by `tierStep` and higher by `tierRise`.\n\nEVERY OTHER TIER IS OFFSET BY HALF A PITCH — `(_ti % 2) * PI / arms` — so candles on the tier above do not sit directly over the ones below. That is one term in the angle expression, and it is the difference between a chandelier and a stack of rings.\n\nTHE RING IS A RING ROW, not a torus row. A Torus is positioned by a POINT and lies flat by construction; a Ring is driven by its AXIS SEGMENT, so the decorative hoop is described by the same vertical axis the column already has — and only the segment's direction and midpoint are read, so its length is free.\n\nTHE PLAN IS A DRAFTING SYMBOL: the spread circle, radial arm strokes, a candle dot per lamp and the column. The candle dots come from `Cups3D` — the same world coordinates the 3D cups were built at — so the symbol and the model cannot drift apart.\n\nDIMENSIONS AT THE DEFAULTS: 0.70 m spread, six lamps on one tier, top at 3.00 m, bottom at 2.14 m, candles at 2.29 m.\n\nWHAT THIS CANNOT DO. Arms are straight tubes — no scroll, no curve, no crystal. The chain is a single cylinder, not links. There is no shade or globe over the lamps.",
